/-!
# Explicit quaternion matrix for the graph normalizer

The rational candidate is half `numerator`. `coordinates` records its action
on the actual integral basis; `gramProduct` clears the intermediate Gram
product. These are numerical data only. The following modules check its
square, integral isometry, quaternion scalar compatibility and the exact
Peirce graph action on the two published generators.

Source: Aschbacher, Sporadic Groups (1994), proof of 49.5, p.283.
The normalizer was obtained by intertwining the two concrete matrix generators
with words lifting J A⁻ᵀ J in their literal modular quotient. No splitting
of the integral block or of its graph extension is used.
-/

